# Trim the docker build context and keep the COPY layer cache stable across docs/CI edits.
# This file governs the multi-stage CI builds run from the repo root
# (`ci/Jenkinsfile`: `docker build -f hashbin-quarkus/src/main/docker/Dockerfile.*-multi-stage .`),
# which compile inside the container and so want no host build output in the context.
# `.git/` is the biggest win (a few MB, grows with history); `docs/`, `scripts/`, and `ci/` are
# never read by the build, so excluding them lets the layer cache survive doc/Jenkinsfile edits.
#
# Note: the single-stage `Dockerfile.jvm`/`Dockerfile.native` (used by `mvn -Dquarkus.container-image.build`)
# run with the *module* directory as context, where `target/` is the artifact they COPY — that
# context is unaffected by this root-level file, so excluding `**/target/` here is safe.

.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
**/.quarkus/
**/target/
*.env
docs/
scripts/
ci/
